Hi mtd/ubifs friends,

First off, thanks for your work, especially providing the backport to
2.6.37. I found that to be very useful.

On my board, I'm able to flash ubifs to nand using u-boot, boot from
that ubifs on nand once and run happily during that time. But then if
I do a power cycle, I encounter a high chance of boot failure (90%).
I've tested that the behavior is consistent on 3 boards. I've attached
serial console logs to show what I observe.

I went through the FAQ, and the free space fixup issue looked close to
my symptoms so I set -F in mkfs.ubifs and pulled the ubifs backport. I
see "UBIFS: free space fixup complete" in the first boot so I think
this is working. I'm pretty sure I must be doing something wrong but
I'm having trouble figuring that out. I would appreciate any
advice/suggestions.

